---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
---

<PageLayout
    title="About - Vincent Foriel"
    description="Background and research of Vincent Foriel, PhD candidate in astrophotonics"
    currentPath={Astro.url.pathname}
>
    <Section>
        <div class="about-header">
            <h1>About</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                PhD candidate in astronomical instrumentation, high-contrast
                imaging and optical simulation
            </p>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section>
        <div class="content-grid">
            <div class="content-main">
                <h2>My Journey</h2>
                <p>
                    Astrophysics has always fascinated me — black holes, neutron
                    stars, the sheer scale of cosmic structures. This passion
                    was fueled by Stephen Hawking's books as much as by works
                    like <em>Star Trek</em> or
                    <em>Interstellar</em>.
                </p>

                <p>
                    I first pursued a computer science degree, a field where I
                    had natural aptitude. But it was through following science
                    communicators and, more surprisingly, creating projectile
                    trajectory systems in Minecraft — trigonometry, basis
                    changes, point physics — that I made peace with math and
                    decided to pivot toward physics.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Today, as a PhD candidate in astrophotonics, I design and
                    analyze instruments for astronomical observation. I adapt to
                    everything — theoretical as well as experimental physics —
                    but I particularly enjoy <strong
                        >computational physics</strong
                    >: from physical simulations to developing human-machine and
                    machine-machine interfaces for scientific or outreach
                    applications.
                </p>

                <h2>My Work Philosophy</h2>
                <p>Four principles guide my daily work:</p>

                <ul class="values-list">
                    <li>
                        <strong>Curiosity first</strong> — Explore, let yourself be
                        surprised, follow an unexpected lead. The best discoveries
                        often come from what you didn't plan to study.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Make it simple</strong> — What is well conceived is
                        clearly expressed. No dark corners, no unnecessarily complex
                        formulas, only simple words and decomposed logic.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Elegance is a feature</strong> — A performant system
                        is not enough. Its elegance, intuitiveness, and the pleasure
                        of using it matter just as much. A well-designed axe head
                        is useless if the handle isn't.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Never do something twice</strong> — Automate everything
                        that can be automated. Scripts, pipelines, CI/CD: every repetitive
                        task deserves to become a reliable, reproducible process.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Organization</h2>
                <p>
                    I rely on project forges — GitHub, GitLab, Redmine,
                    OpenProject — to structure my work: issue management, code
                    reviews, integrated documentation. This approach lets me
                    work effectively with
                    <strong>autonomy</strong> while making collaboration seamless
                    when opportunities arise.
                </p>
            </div>

            <aside class="content-sidebar">
                <div class="sidebar-card">
                    <h3>🎨 Jack of all trades</h3>
                    <p class="interests-text">
                        I love learning and exploring new fields. Piano today,
                        Japanese tomorrow, 3D printing next week — the subject
                        doesn't matter, curiosity is what drives me.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="sidebar-card fun-fact">
                    <h3>🎮 Fun fact</h3>
                    <p>
                        It was while building a projectile system in Minecraft —
                        point physics, trigonometry — that I decided to pursue
                        physics studies.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        That project gave birth to
                        <a href="/en/associations">Altearn</a> and
                        <a
                            href="https://docs.mcbookshelf.dev/en/latest/"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">Bookshelf</a
                        >, a real Minecraft development library featuring math
                        and physics tools.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </Section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
    .about-header {
        max-width: 65ch;
        margin-inline: auto;
        text-align: center;
        margin-block-end: var(--space-12);
    }

    .about-header h1 {
        font-size: var(--text-4xl);
        margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
    }

    .lead {
        font-size: var(--text-xl);
        color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    }

    .content-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 300px;
        gap: var(--space-12);
        align-items: start;
    }

    .content-main {
        padding: var(--space-8);
        background-color: var(--color-background-secondary);
        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    }

    .content-main h2 {
        font-size: var(--text-2xl);
        margin-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-4);
    }

    .content-main h2:first-of-type {
        margin-block-start: 0;
    }

    .content-main p {
        margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
        color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    }

    .expertise-list,
    .values-list {
        list-style: none;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: var(--space-4);
        margin-block: var(--space-6);
    }

    .expertise-list li,
    .values-list li {
        padding-inline-start: var(--space-6);
        position: relative;
        color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    }

    .expertise-list li::before,
    .values-list li::before {
        content: "→";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        color: var(--color-primary);
        font-weight: 600;
    }

    .content-sidebar {
        position: sticky;
        top: calc(var(--space-16) + 60px);
        align-self: start;
    }

    .sidebar-card {
        padding: var(--space-6);
        background-color: var(--color-background-secondary);
        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
        margin-block-end: var(--space-6);
    }

    .sidebar-card h3 {
        font-size: var(--text-lg);
        margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
    }

    .sidebar-intro {
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
        color: var(--color-text-secondary);
        margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
        font-style: italic;
    }

    .interests-list {
        list-style: none;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: var(--space-2);
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
        color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    }

    .interests-list li {
        padding-inline-start: 0;
    }

    .inspirations-text {
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
        color: var(--color-text-secondary);
        margin: 0;
    }

    .fun-fact {
        background: linear-gradient(
            135deg,
            var(--color-background-secondary) 0%,
            color-mix(
                    in srgb,
                    var(--color-primary) 10%,
                    var(--color-background-secondary)
                )
                100%
        );
        border-left: 3px solid var(--color-primary);
    }

    .fun-fact p {
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
        color: var(--color-text-secondary);
        margin: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1024px) {
        .content-grid {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .content-sidebar {
            position: static;
        }
    }
</style>
